+   "source": "## 5. Logging the blends as experiment runs — and their per-fold AUC spread\n\nUp to here every strategy was scored on a single **pooled** OOF ROC-AUC. But the\nbase runs are all ranked on their **per-fold** AUC (mean ± std), and the fold std\nis ≈ **0.0009** — larger than the ~+0.0003 a blend buys over the best single\nmodel. `docs/technical_review.md` §2.2 makes the point directly: *\"report the\nblend's per-fold OOF AUC (mean ± std), not just the pooled number, and state\nplainly whether the gain exceeds CV noise.\"*\n\nSo we give each headline blend the same treatment as a base run: score it on every\ncanonical seed-42 fold, and **log it as a first-class `experiments/runs.csv`\nentry** — which records `fold_roc_auc_mean` / `fold_roc_auc_std` for free, makes\nthe blend submittable, and lets it sit on the same leaderboard as the base models.\n\nThe machinery lives in `src/blending.py` (so the notebook and the unattended\n`scripts/run_blend_logging.py` build *identical* blends):\n\n- `build_headline_blends(...)` constructs the six (rank-mean curated; moderate-C\n  curated logit stack; the carried-forward best logit stack on the full pool;\n  hill-climb curated; best-softmax mean; the 50-trial Optuna LightGBM stack).\n- `save_blend_run(...)` writes a blend as a run. A blend has no training parquet,\n  so a few columns take blend conventions: `data_version=\"blend_v1\"` (a sentinel,\n  not an FE recipe), `data_hash` = the canonical train parquet (the shared OOF row\n  ordering), `parent_run_id=\"\"` (N parents — the member list + weights live in\n  `params.json`), `model_class` = a synthetic scheme name, `n_features` = the\n  number of member columns. For the rank-mean blend (a rank scale, not a\n  probability) `oof_accuracy` is logged as NaN.\n\nThe cell below **displays** the per-fold table (read it against the ~0.0009 noise\nfloor). Actual logging + Kaggle submission is done **once** by\n`scripts/run_blend_logging.py --submit`, so re-running this notebook never\ndouble-writes rows.",
+   "metadata": {}
+  },
